  "articleBody": "Ever finished framing a new partition wall only to find it's a bit... wobbly or bowed? You're not alone, it's a super common issue that often comes down to a few overlooked details during the framing process. A big one is not accounting for the shortest floor-to-ceiling measurement across the entire wall. If you cut all your studs to one length, you'll run into trouble when different spots have slightly varied heights. Another common culprit is skipping the proper layout and not checking for plumb as you go. It's really easy to just nail things in place and hope for the best, but taking the extra time to mark everything precisely and use a level will save you a headache later. Not shimming properly before fastening can also lead to a crooked wall. You need to make sure everything is tight and true before you commit. Sometimes, trying to tackle a complex wall with existing uneven framing or special deflection needs can be really tricky, and that's when calling in a pro like HH Remodeling can make all the difference. We can help ensure your wall is perfectly straight and solid.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}